    /// Read a recorded deposit
    ///
    /// Returns what is known about a deposit: whether it has been credited, for how much when it has, and the Lighter account it created once there is one.
    /// This is the gate of the registration flow, and the only reader of it in this API. A first deposit is what creates the account, so a client records the deposit, polls this, and continues as soon as account_index is set. There is no deposit-details screen.
    /// The moment itself is Lighter's to report, and this endpoint asks it: a record with no account_index is answered by resolving the address against Lighter live, rather than from what the next scheduled check will write. A client with its own Lighter integration can therefore learn the same thing without this call, one hop earlier. What is only here is the deposit while it is still on its way: the pending row, the amount that was declared -- Lighter keeps only what arrived, so "expected N, got M" can be answered from nowhere else -- and the unfunded verdict.
    /// Answered to the wallet the deposit belongs to. The deposit_id was the whole authorisation once, and is not any more: an id leaks — into a log, a crash report, an analytics event — and it can also be asked for, since recording the same transaction again returns the deposit that already exists, id included. A deposit of another wallet answers 404 rather than 403, because telling those apart would confirm that the id exists.
